Subject: [PATCH] tests/libfuzzer: run dav1d's one-time init in LLVMFuzzerInitialize

dav1d_open() runs init_internal() through pthread_once() on its first
call: the inter-intra wedge masks, the intra edge tree and the QM tables
(about 2.5M wasm instructions). In the fuzzer that cost lands in the first
input, so every fresh process / fresh instance pays it on its first input
and coverage tools that run each input on a fresh instance see a 2.8x
higher per-input cost than the persistent fuzzer. Open and close one
decoder in LLVMFuzzerInitialize() with the same thread settings as the
per-input path; the per-input dav1d_open() then takes the pthread_once
fast path, as it already does for every input after the first.

Upstream context: dav1d tracks issues and MRs on code.videolan.org, which
gh cannot search; the GitHub mirror has none (checked 2026-11-20).

diff --git a/tests/libfuzzer/dav1d_fuzzer.c b/tests/libfuzzer/dav1d_fuzzer.c
index 502ee22b..b2c00a90 100644
--- a/tests/libfuzzer/dav1d_fuzzer.c
+++ b/tests/libfuzzer/dav1d_fuzzer.c
@@ -84,6 +84,15 @@ int LLVMFuzzerInitialize(int *argc, char ***argv) {
 
     *argc = i;
 
+    // dav1d_open() builds the static tables (wedge masks, intra edge tree,
+    // QM tables) on its first call; do that here, not in the first input.
+    Dav1dSettings settings;
+    Dav1dContext *ctx = NULL;
+    dav1d_default_settings(&settings);
+    settings.max_frame_delay = settings.n_threads = 1;
+    if (dav1d_open(&ctx, &settings) == 0)
+        dav1d_close(&ctx);
+
     return 0;
 }
 
